                    insight_pivot:          `Pivot achieved: you ran the genuine portfolio realignment — launched the emerging-skill topics, matched delivery to audience, partnered for speed where the cycle was tight, won the custom mandates on value, and built a demand-monitoring loop. Margin cleared the 32% hurdle, fill recovered toward break-even, NPS rose, and the anchor clients are signed.`,
                    insight_legacy:         `Legacy trap: you kept defending the proven face-to-face functional catalog instead of pivoting toward demand-driven emerging skills. The core that filled at 62% kept filling at 62% — fill and NPS eroded together while a global platform out-priced you on the same content.`,
                    insight_discount:       `Margin bought away: you restored fill by discounting, but the open-program margin fell below the 32% target and the market learned to wait for the price cut. Fill purchased with margin is not a recovery — it is the next crisis, deferred.`,
                    insight_missed:         `Missed the cycle: you insisted on building the new capabilities entirely in-house, and by the time they were ready the anchor clients had signed with a faster global provider. Build/buy/partner is a speed decision as much as a margin one — and the budget cycle does not wait.`,
                    insight_underpriced:    `Margin bought away: you won the custom logos by pricing below the 32% hurdle, locking scarce senior faculty into low-margin work. Winning the mandate is not the same as winning the economics — the opportunity cost of that faculty was the higher-margin open portfolio.`,
                    insight_onesize:        `One-size delivery: you imposed a single mode on the whole catalog instead of matching face-to-face, online and blended to topic and audience. Either you walked into the platforms' price strength online, or you capped scale and clashed with executives' schedules face-to-face — and NPS paid for it.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed pivot: some of the realignment landed, but topics, delivery, pricing and partnership did not fully reinforce each other — enough seams for margin, fill or NPS to lag and for the board to question whether the catalog is truly ahead of demand.`,
                    insight_margin_low:     `Contribution margin never cleared the 32% target: discounting, underpricing or matching the platform's price kept the portfolio below the board's mandate, eroding the very margin the pivot was meant to defend.`,
                    insight_fill_low:       `Portfolio fill rate stayed below break-even: the catalog never fully realigned to where demand is, so seats kept going unfilled and the open programs kept losing money below the 80% break-even.`,
                    insight_nps_low:        `Learner NPS stayed low: the pivot did not give learners and sponsors a reason to advocate — and NPS is the cheapest acquisition channel, so weak NPS is tomorrow's enrollment shortfall.`,
                    insight_custom_lost:    `You did not secure the full custom mandate: by underpricing, over-pricing, or failing the outcome-measurement condition, you left part of the S/ 6M of anchor spend on the table for a competitor.`,
                    insight_monitor:        `You built a standing demand-monitoring loop: employer signals, RFP patterns, competitor pricing and NPS now feed a quarterly grow/fix/retire review — the discipline that keeps the catalog from ever lagging the market again.`,

                    hint_discount:          `You are bleeding margin — discounting or matching the platform's price has dragged you below the 32% target. Hold price, differentiate on applied value, and stop training the market to wait for the cut.`,
                    hint_legacy:            `You are defending the legacy catalog — fill is stuck because the programs answer questions a 2026 executive can buy cheaper online. Launch the emerging-skill topics and retire the low-fill seminars before the next intake.`,
                    hint_missed:            `Building everything in-house is too slow for this cycle — the anchor clients will sign elsewhere. Partner or license for the emerging-skill gaps to be fast to demand, and build in-house only where you already have depth.`,
                    hint_underpriced:       `You won the logos but below the 32% hurdle — scarce faculty are locked into low-margin custom work. Price the next mandate to clear the hurdle on value, and weigh the opportunity cost of the open portfolio.`,
